<!--
Add these keys to your Xcode project's Info.plist (or the "Info" tab of your target's
build settings, which is where modern Xcode templates keep them by default).

Both are required or the Pairing screen will crash/fail silently at runtime:
- NSCameraUsageDescription: required to scan the Desktop Companion's QR code.
- NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription: required because the paired connection talks to the
  Companion over your local Wi-Fi/USB-shared network, not the public internet.
-->
<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
<string>RustGestalt needs the camera to scan the pairing code shown by the Desktop Companion app.</string>

<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
<string>RustGestalt connects to the Desktop Companion app over your local network to read and apply device settings.</string>
